item.ams_core.desc1=A modified undefined state of spacetime
item.ams_core.desc10=that matter into pure energy. That means
item.ams_core.desc11=you're actively contributing to the destruction
item.ams_core.desc12=of another dimension, sucking it dry like a
item.ams_core.desc13=juicebox.
item.ams_core.desc14=That dimension probably sucked, anyways. I
item.ams_core.desc15=bet it was full of wasps or some crap, man,
item.ams_core.desc16=I hate these things.
item.ams_core.desc17=A star collapsing in on itself, mere nanoseconds
item.ams_core.desc18=away from being turned into a black hole,
item.ams_core.desc19=frozen in time. If I didn't know better I
item.ams_core.desc2=used to aid in inter-gluon fusion and
item.ams_core.desc20=would say this is some deep space magic
item.ams_core.desc21=bullcrap some guy made up to sound intellectual.
item.ams_core.desc22=Probably Steve from accounting. You still owe me
item.ams_core.desc23=ten bucks.
item.ams_core.desc24=Yeah I'm not even gonna question that one.
item.ams_core.desc25=...am I even holding this right?
item.ams_core.desc26=It's a small metal thing. I dunno where it's from
item.ams_core.desc27=or what it does, maybe they found it on a
item.ams_core.desc28=junkyard and sold it as some kind of antique
item.ams_core.desc29=artifact. If it weren't for the fact that I can
item.ams_core.desc3=spacetime annihilation. Yes, this destroys
item.ams_core.desc30=actually stuff this into some great big laser
item.ams_core.desc31=reactor thing, I'd probably bring it back to where
item.ams_core.desc32=it belongs. In the trash.
item.ams_core.desc4=the universe itself, slowly but steadily,
item.ams_core.desc5=but at least you can power your toaster with
item.ams_core.desc6=this, so it's all good.
item.ams_core.desc7=A cloud of billions of nano-wormholes which
item.ams_core.desc8=deliberately fail at tunneling matter from
item.ams_core.desc9=another dimension, rather it converts all
